1145 "Writing down our triple integral as a mixed integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}16x\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{x-y}16x\\,dz]dA.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ and $y$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{x-y}16x\\,dz]dA & ={∬}_{D}[16xz]_{z=0}^{z=x-y}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}16x(x-y)\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now evaluate the double integral above over the region $D$ in the $xy$-plane shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062541/assets/bddbd1c97fe8cd74f9903dec340495f04401323b8e1236680c57c13b18069eb4.png)\n\nWe can evaluate our double integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}16x(x-y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{3/2}{\\int }_{2x-3}^{0}16x(x-y)\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3/2}16x[{\\int }_{2x-3}^{0}(x-y)\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3/2}16x{[xy-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=2x-3}^{y=0}dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3/2}16x(0-x(2x-3)+\\frac{1}{2}(2x-3)^{2})\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3/2}8x(-4{x}^{2}+6x+4{x}^{2}-12x+9)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3/2}8x(-6x+9)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3/2}-48{x}^{2}+72x\\,dx \\\\  & ={[-16{x}^{3}+36{x}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=3/2} \\\\  & =-16{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{3}+36{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =-54+81 \\\\  & =27\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535331 true] [17592186344251 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344252 13194139535331 true] [17592186344251 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344253 13194139535331 true] [17592186344251 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344254 13194139535331 true] [17592186344251 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344255 13194139535331 true] [17592186344251 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344256 13194139535331 true] [17592186344251 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535331 true] [17592186344251 1041 "selection" 13194139535331 true] [17592186344251 1104 #edb/ref 17592186344256 13194139535331 true] [17592186344251 1110 #uuid "43b407a5-736c-5cc5-b16f-d2eb5973afa2" 13194139535331 true] [17592186344252 1034 "\\frac{9}{2