shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the top one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" 13194139535331 true] [17592186344264 1113 #uuid "d0333962-96ee-5729-b372-72df4a42f181" 13194139535331 true] [17592186344264 1145 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062541/assets/9002d6f1e55a734e410fc85111816294ed037c4a4139e9bc8bceb53c62daeeb6.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type I region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1+x},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062541/assets/31f2ff96afa1248427c1a6dd5074c47190c70983d7c0d5dfdd3def8bd883aef8.png)\n\nHence, we can express the region $R$ as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1+x}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1+x}{y}^{2}\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ and $y$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1+x}{y}^{2}\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1+x}{y}^{2}\\,dz]dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{y}^{2}z]_{z=0}^{z=1+x}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}(1+x)\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}(1+x)\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}(1+x){y}^{2}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(1+x){[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(1+x)(\\frac{8}{3}-0)\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}1+x\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}1+x\\,dx & =\\frac{8}{3}{[x+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=3} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}(3+\\frac{9}{2})-0 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535331 true] [17592186344265 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344266 13194139535331 true] [17592186344265 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344267 13194139535331 true] [17592186344265 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344268 13194139535331 true] [17592186344265 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344269 13194139535331 true] [17592186344265 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344270 13194139535331 true] [17592186344265 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535331 true] [17592186344265 1041 "selection" 13194139535331 true] [17592186344265 1104 #edb/ref 17592186344266 13194139535331 true] [17592186344265 1110 #uuid "f4b50245-c552-5059-92ef-7e0deb413917" 13194139535331 true] [17592186344266 1034 "20" 13194139535331 true] [17592186344266 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535331 true] [17592186344266 1111 #uuid "6a52852b-a96a-51f5-8ef9-3e38a42fa102" 13194139535331 true] [17592186344267 1034 "10" 13194139535331 true] [17592186344267 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535331 true] [17592186344267 1111 #uuid "da264142-bb99-5c5f-82ad-67257f9ada07" 13194139535331 true] [17592186344268 1034 "15" 13194139535331 true] [17592186344268 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535331 true] [17592186344268 1111 #uuid "7ef88df3-20f5-5f91-bc5e-d23f734d4fbf" 13194139535331 true] [17592186344269 1034 "25" 13194139535331 true] [17592186344269 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535331 true] [17592186344269 1111 #uuid "fcebbc4f-8788-5215-93bf-3c22ce2d7266" 13194139535331 true] [17592186344270 1034 "5" 13194139535331 true] [17592186344270 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535331 true] [17592186344270 1111 #uuid "3fd4020e-613b-55ee-96bd-3fd762ea2b4c" 13194139535331 true] [17592186344271 1017 #edb/ref 17592186344272 13194139535331 true] [17592186344271 1089 "q-161519" 13194139535331 true] [17592186344271 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535331 true] [17592186344271 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062541/assets/91e8b39eb1bf181ceaf5b33b25fbb5ed0fa3ca7f7c1f0bb830c3337f142eb1dd.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}{z}^{2}\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the top one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" 13194139535331 true] [17592186344271 1113 #uuid "784ab118-b653-5844-8b14-75abf3ee5fde" 13194139535331 true] [17592186344271 1145 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062541/assets/5c8b476bceea5225cd230bd6e881706269b6eeda415503266e96e6e3c676b237.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type I region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1+y},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062541/assets/31f2ff96afa1248427c1a6dd5074c47190c70983d7c0d5dfdd3def8bd883aef8.png)\n\nHence, we can express the region $R$ as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1+y}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1+y}{z}^{2}\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ and $y$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1+y}{z}^{2}\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1+y}{z}^{2}\\,dz]dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{{z}^{3}}{3}]}_{z=0}^{z=1+y}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{(1+y)^{3}}{3}\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{(1+y)^{3}}{3}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{(1+y)^{3}}{3}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[\\frac{(1+y)^{4}}{12}]}_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{12}(81-1)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{20}{3}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{20}{3}\\,dx & ={[\\frac{20}{3}x]}_{x=0}^{x=3} \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535331 true] [17592186344272 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344273 13194139535331 true] [17592186344272 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344274 13194139535331 true] [17592186344272 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344275 13194139535331 true] [17592186344272 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344276 13194139535331 true] [17592186344272 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344277 13194139535331 true] [17592186344272 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535331 true] [17592186344272 1041 "selection" 13194139535331 true] [17592186344272 1104 #edb/ref 17592186344274 13194139535331 true] [17592186344272 1110 #uuid "37dbdfc5-662a-5d5a-bfd5-bd48b8771e97" 13194139535331 true] [17592186344273 1034 "\\frac{9}{2}" 13194139535331 true] [17592186344273 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535331 true] [17592186344273 1111 #uuid "fe3afb71-feb2-5afa-979b-b37714cb5fb3" 13194139535331 true] [17592186344274 1034 "20" 13194139535331 true] [17592186344274 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535331 true] [17592186344274 1111 #uuid "8af50fd0-fb12-5d76-8331-beb159dc3f37" 13194139535331 true] [17592186344275 1034 "15" 13194139535331 true] [17592186344275 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535331 true] [17592186344275 1111 #uuid "1439981a-8dcc-5d25-ae6d-5305e2f37d3a" 13194139535331 true] [17592186344276 1034 "\\frac{27}{4}" 13194139535331 true] [17592186344276 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535331 true] [17592186344276 